        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p19-q1-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{c-d}+\\dfrac{1}{d-c}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$0$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{c-d}+\\frac1{d-c}&=\\frac1{c-d}-\\frac1{c-d}\\\\\\frac1{c-d}+\\frac1{d-c}&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          },
          {
            "id": "p19-q1-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$\\dfrac{p}{p-q}+\\dfrac{q}{q-p}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$1$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac p{p-q}+\\frac q{q-p}&=\\frac p{p-q}-\\frac q{p-q}\\\\\\frac p{p-q}+\\frac q{q-p}&=\\frac{p-q}{p-q}\\\\\\frac p{p-q}+\\frac q{q-p}&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 43
          },
          {
            "id": "p19-q1-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{a+\\frac1b}+\\dfrac{1}{b+\\frac1a}-\\dfrac{1}{\\frac12a+\\frac12b}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{a^2+b^2-2}{(ab+1)(a+b)}$\n\nClear the fractions inside the denominators, then use a common denominator.",
              "worked": "Let $E$ denote the given expression.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=\\frac b{ab+1}+\\frac a{ab+1}-\\frac2{a+b}\\\\E&=\\frac{a+b}{ab+1}-\\frac2{a+b}\\\\E&=\\frac{(a+b)^2-2(ab+1)}{(ab+1)(a+b)}\\\\E&=\\frac{a^2+2ab+b^2-2ab-2}{(ab+1)(a+b)}\\\\E&=\\frac{a^2+b^2-2}{(ab+1)(a+b)}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 77
          },
          {
            "id": "p19-q1-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$\\dfrac{b+c}{b-c}+\\dfrac{b-c}{b+c}+\\dfrac{4bc}{c^2-b^2}$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\dfrac{2(b-c)}{b+c}$",
              "worked": "Let $E$ denote the given expression. Since $c^2-b^2=-(b-c)(b+c)$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=\\frac{(b+c)^2+(b-c)^2-4bc}{(b-c)(b+c)}\\\\E&=\\frac{2b^2-4bc+2c^2}{(b-c)(b+c)}\\\\E&=\\frac{2(b-c)^2}{(b-c)(b+c)}\\\\E&=\\frac{2(b-c)}{b+c}.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 70
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p19-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{b+c}{(b-a)(c-a)}+\\dfrac{c+a}{(c-b)(a-b)}+\\dfrac{a+b}{(a-c)(b-c)}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$\n\nUse a common denominator and expand the differences of squares in the numerator.",
          "worked": "Let $E$ denote the given expression and $D=(b-a)(c-a)(c-b)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}E&=\\frac{(b+c)(c-b)-(c+a)(c-a)+(a+b)(b-a)}D\\\\E&=\\frac{c^2-b^2-(c^2-a^2)+(b^2-a^2)}D\\\\E&=0.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 59
      }
    ]
